From 4d7c98a23662c5757f79ad67ce5efdfb4d69bf6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 16:03:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HiBreak: cycle the radio of a SIM stuck out of service

The MediaTek modem can stay unregistered on WWAN CS and PS for hours,
repeating EMM attach reject 112, while it still measures cells of the
SIM's home PLMN; only a radio power cycle (airplane mode) recovers it,
and stock has no automatic recovery.

Per phone, when the radio is on and desired on, the SIM is loaded with
an active subscription and WWAN voice and data are both unregistered,
arm a non-wakeup alarm: 5 min, then 10, 30 and every 60 min while still
stuck; reset the backoff once WWAN voice or data registers. At fire
time re-check everything, require no call, emergency state or network
scan on any phone, and a home PLMN cell (IMSI MCC/MNC, EHPLMN, HPLMN)
in the cell info list from one rate-limited request. The cycle reuses
the data stall radio restart, ServiceStateTracker.powerOffRadioSafely();
the radio stays desired on and powers on again. Bigme HiBreak mt6877
only.

Kill switch: setprop persist.radio.hibreak_oos_recovery false. Logs in
the radio buffer under HBPC_OOS_RECOVERY; the non-persistent
ril.hibreak.oos_recovery.<phoneId> holds '<last action> <cycles>
<uptime-ms>' for the last reset, skip or cycle.

